# redis-py 8.0 defaults to RESP3 on the wire, which breaks channels_redis's
# blocking-pop channel layer (BZPOPMIN -> "Timeout reading from redis") and
# takes down ALL WebSockets (terminal, live status). channels-redis only
# declares `redis>=4.6` with no upper bound, so an unpinned build floats to
# the newest major -- this regressed prod on 2026-06-13. Cap below 8.0 until
# channels_redis supports RESP3. See https://github.com/redis/redis-py/issues/4091
